{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088334-how-do-you-remove-nightmare","id":1088334,"title":"How do you remove Nightmare","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-05T09:34:01-07:00","id":1088334,"title":"How do you remove Nightmare","content":"What Nightmares do, besides replacing your casting Dice Pool? What replacing of Dice Pool even does?<br /> <br /> How do you get rid of Nightmares?<br /> <br /> The paragraph on Nightmares isn't very conclusive. Where can I read more, if I missed something? Could you clarify on my questions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T10:34:27-07:00","id":1088372,"title":"","content":"P. 275: <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Imbalance </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">When a character\u2019s Nightmare rating reaches 10, the player removes all the Nightmare points from the character sheet and then marks an imbalance by circling the character\u2019s rightmost Willpower box (underneath the last dot of Willpower, reading left to right). The Willpower point represented by that box functions normally, except that the character suffers a Bedlam Threshold (p. 294) if she spends the Imbalanced point of Willpower. If all of a character\u2019s Willpower becomes Imbalanced, she is lost to Bedlam. Marking an Imbalanced Willpower also regains one point of Glamour. </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T12:18:16-07:00","id":1088411,"title":"","content":"And the way to change an imbalanced willpower dot back to a normal willpower dot is through an Epiphany.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T12:36:18-07:00","id":1088424,"title":"","content":"Am I right in also thinking that the Bedlam Thresholds recur every time that Willpower point is spent? Or does the imbalance disappear upon spending it? I'm guessing the former, although I'm not sure it says explicitly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T12:43:36-07:00","id":1088425,"title":"","content":"Im going to miss Banality Therapy...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T14:02:26-07:00","id":1088480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088334-how-do-you-remove-nightmare?p=1088425#post1088425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im going to miss Banality Therapy...</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an AP for that. <br /> <br /> Autumn People: solving fae problems, one Stigma at a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T14:28:31-07:00","id":1088494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088334-how-do-you-remove-nightmare?p=1088424#post1088424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I right in also thinking that the Bedlam Thresholds recur every time that Willpower point is spent? Or does the imbalance disappear upon spending it? I'm guessing the former, although I'm not sure it says explicitly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every time that particular Willpower point is spent. Else it would be simple to circumvent gaining more Banality than that one Imbalance Willpower, by simply spending that one point as soon as it turns imbalanced.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> And yes, that means that while the first Imbalanced Willpower might not hurt much, the severity grows exponentially - more Imbalanced Willpower means closer to Undoing, and it also means that your usable willpower pool more and more comes with Bedlam Threshold hits when you use too many of its temporary Willpower points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-05-2017, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T15:10:24-07:00","id":1088508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088334-how-do-you-remove-nightmare?p=1088494#post1088494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every time that particular Willpower point is spent. Else it would be simple to circumvent gaining more Banality than that one Imbalance Willpower, by simply spending that one point as soon as it turns imbalanced.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> And yes, that means that while the first Imbalanced Willpower might not hurt much, the severity grows exponentially - more Imbalanced Willpower means closer to Undoing, and it also means that your usable willpower pool more and more comes with Bedlam Threshold hits when you use too many of its temporary Willpower points.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I was thinking. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T17:43:08-07:00","id":1088568,"title":"","content":"So, the only way to get rid of Nightmare-inducedeffects is rising them up? Noted.<br /> <br /> That still doesn't answer my question, why should I replace my casting dice with Nightmare and what it does?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T17:55:41-07:00","id":1088570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088334-how-do-you-remove-nightmare?p=1088568#post1088568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the only way to get rid of Nightmare-inducedeffects is rising them up? Noted.<br /> <br /> That still doesn't answer my question, why should I replace my casting dice with Nightmare and what it does?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You have to replace casting dice with Nightmare dice. And every time a nightmare die rolls a 10 your nightmare pool goes up by 1. So if you have any Nightmare dice, every time you use a Cantrip you risk getting closer to Bedlam.<br /> <br /> It might seem a bit off because it's a fairly slow progression that would take multiple sessions to become a real problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T18:21:41-07:00","id":1088578,"title":"","content":"Every time you use a Cantrip you risk getting closer to Bedlam. Botches raise it too.<br /> <br /> But there is no way to lower Nightmares other than raising them. <br /> <br /> ...and they do nothing, other than helping you to get closer to Bedlam. Which you won't fall into unless you spend that Point of Willpower. <br /> <br /> As is now, the Nightmares require a lot of maintenance, but provide too little amusement in return. <br /> <br /> Maybe adding some Nightmare Triggers in the vein of c2ed. Every time your Nightmare goes up you enjoy the &quot;blessings&quot; of Bedlam for a short period of time. Chimerical hauntings, compulsions, Firchlis acting drunkedly, minor hallucinations, etc. Dunno.<br /> <br /> I'll need to check DA:F and CtL on how they did similar stuff, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-06-2017, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T18:35:51-07:00","id":1088581,"title":"","content":"I think just porting over the rules that 2e Changeling the Dreaming used for Nightmare dice could give you what you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T18:42:59-07:00","id":1088584,"title":"","content":"System tinkering it is, then!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T03:35:22-07:00","id":1088682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088334-how-do-you-remove-nightmare?p=1088578#post1088578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every time you use a Cantrip you risk getting closer to Bedlam. Botches raise it too.<br /> <br /> But there is no way to lower Nightmares other than raising them. <br /> <br /> ...and they do nothing, other than helping you to get closer to Bedlam. Which you won't fall into unless you spend that Point of Willpower. <br /> <br /> As is now, the Nightmares require a lot of maintenance, but provide too little amusement in return. <br /> <br /> Maybe adding some Nightmare Triggers in the vein of c2ed. Every time your Nightmare goes up you enjoy the &quot;blessings&quot; of Bedlam for a short period of time. Chimerical hauntings, compulsions, Firchlis acting drunkedly, minor hallucinations, etc. Dunno.<br /> <br /> I'll need to check DA:F and CtL on how they did similar stuff, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of agree with this. The permanent Nightmare imbalance doesn't really come into play unless you spend Willpower points. It probably should cause a Nightmare trigger as in 2e, which lasts for up to a scene. This recurs whenever the imbalanced Willpower point is spent. It would have to be removed like Quiet in Mage--with sufficient effort and restraint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T04:12:35-07:00","id":1088694,"title":"","content":"From what I am reading, that's pretty much what happens when you spend an Imbalanced Willpower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T04:37:01-07:00","id":1088698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088334-how-do-you-remove-nightmare?p=1088694#post1088694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I am reading, that's pretty much what happens when you spend an Imbalanced Willpower?</div> </div> </div> </div>D'oh. You're absolutely right. I started writing that post suggesting that it should cause temporary flaws that follow the character around, like Paradox Flaws, and which grow in severity as imbalance increases. Then I changed my mind and suggested exactly what the book does. My bad.<br /> <br /> A system of Nightmare Flaws, like Paradox Flaws, would potentially be more interesting and have greater consequences. But you'd need a better way for reducing permanent Nightmare (maybe you can sacrifice a dot of Glamour or go on a quest).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T06:33:37-07:00","id":1088730,"title":"","content":"Before in c2e, you could take Nightmares instead of Banality and there was a pretty neat way of getting rid of it. Now, I'll have to think something around. Going for a quest i.e. addressing Dreaming should only make Nightmares worse, as I understand it. <br /> <br /> It's simply a Glamour Imbalance in kithain's &quot;Chi&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's not like you can undertake Banal quests. =))<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T08:57:44-07:00","id":1088767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088334-how-do-you-remove-nightmare?p=1088730#post1088730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before in c2e, you could take Nightmares instead of Banality and there was a pretty neat way of getting rid of it. Now, I'll have to think something around. Going for a quest i.e. addressing Dreaming should only make Nightmares worse, as I understand it. <br /> <br /> It's simply a Glamour Imbalance in kithain's &amp;quot;Chi&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> It's not like you can undertake Banal quests. =))</div> </div> </div> </div>You could, but that would make for a very boring game session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T10:09:30-07:00","id":1088788,"title":"","content":"It might be not, if this how pooka Childlings imagine Big Bad Banality. Or Quests, for that matter.<br /> <br /> It'll fail to live up to its purpose, but well. Not every endeavor should succeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T00:38:00-07:00","id":1089034,"title":"","content":"Make friends with a Liam. ;D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:19:13-07:00","id":1089376,"title":"","content":"Heya! I did some work on the design for Nightmare, Imbalance, and Bedlam in C20. I may be able to offer some perspective on how and why those parts of the game were changed.<br /> <br /> Nightmare dice in C2e were a Banailty mechanic, giving the players a release valve, but 10 Nightmare would result in a permanent Banality. There was no way to get rid of Nightmare in C2e other than rolling \u20181\u2019s or accumulating 10 point which converted to permanent Banality. Bedlam in C2e had no mechanical system at all (\u201cThe Storyteller has complete control over the process of Bedlam\u201d).<br /> <br /> One of the design goals for C20 was giving Bedlam an equivalent presence in the game mechanics as Banality (as a condition, not necessarily a temper). Additionally, Nightmare seemed out of place as pathway to Banality what with Nightmares being a type of dream. The perspective we took was basically that Nightmare as a concept felt more in tune with dreaming gone wrong (Bedlam) then no dreams at all (Banality).<br /> <br /> All of this led to a design for the same type of accumulation system for Nightmare, but with the result of 10 points being Imbalance as a gateway to Bedlam Thresholds, removing the arbitration of Bedlam from simple Storyteller fiat. By introducing Nightmare as an element of the path to Bedlam, we could tie it into Unleashing and also give the players a choice to reduce the difficulty of cantrips by willingingly taking on more Nightmare dice.<br /> <br /> As it stands, Nightmare is a slow(ish) build to Imbalances, which are a slow(ish) build to Bedlam. Bedlam, like Undoing, is a character ending event, so we made a conscious choice to have the systemic progression to Bedlam feel ever-present (Nightmare dice get rolled frequently) but to have the actual descent into Bedlam include some player agency (Unleashing, spending Imbalanced Willpower, pursuing Epiphany to mitigate Imbalance).<br /> <br /> That's the reader's digest on the design process. If you and your group enjoyed Nightmare tied to Banality, and liked Bedlam as a pure narrative device, follow your dreams! Err, or nightmares I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13387-jonsan","name":"jonsan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:27:19-07:00","id":1089380,"title":"","content":"I for one am happy to see Bedlam given a mechanic.<br /> <br /> That said, I can still see embracing Bedlam as a way to resist Banality. Kinda like getting addicted to stimulants to resist tiredness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:54:58-07:00","id":1089399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jonsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088334-how-do-you-remove-nightmare?p=1089376#post1089376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bedlam in C2e had no mechanical system at all (\u201cThe Storyteller has complete control over the process of Bedlam\u201d)</div> </div> </div> </div>But there was a pretty clear mechanic. &quot;If most of the [<i>following statements</i>] are true, you're probably in Bedlam or heading right there.&quot; Once you reached first or second stage, you'd have to change something in your life or <b>else</b>.<br /> <br /> Also, there were nothing, that prevented you from playing your character on Bedlam III. It would surely colour every interaction with others, but it's not impossible.<br /> <br /> Actually by marking off Willpower from left to right, I could make Bedlam coming a bit faster (but allowing strong-willed characters to hold longer). But by returning Nightmare Flaws I'd allow some degree of Nightmare release (instead of death spiral, where more Nightmares make more Nightmares).<br /> <br /> Also, surges of wild uncontrolled Glamour tainting your magic is fun!<br /> <br /> But it might need some tinkering to make sure, that Bedlam Thresholds are actually reachable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-08-2017, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:56:55-07:00","id":1089404,"title":"","content":"The other question is. Does Nightmare Temper has anything to do with Nightmare Legacies, Nightmare Realms, etc. or it's just the term, entirely unconnected from Fomorians?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T15:20:15-07:00","id":1089425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088334-how-do-you-remove-nightmare?p=1089404#post1089404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other question is. Does Nightmare Temper has anything to do with Nightmare Legacies, Nightmare Realms, etc. or it's just the term, entirely unconnected from Fomorians?</div> </div> </div> </div>The stat and Nightmare dice are distinct from the legacies and realm. From a design perspective, using a term like Nightmare for multiple purposes that don't intersect is a no-no, but there were several points in the design process for C20 were we had to strike a balance between respecting the previous edition and adding/changing things.<br /> <br /> As for the Nightmare Flaws, adding them back in as consequence when a Nightmare die rolls '1' sounds fun, but it would significantly slow the progression toward Bedlam. If you run it that way put up a post and let me know how it plays, I'd be interested to hear about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13387-jonsan","name":"jonsan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T13:21:44-07:00","id":1089919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jonsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088334-how-do-you-remove-nightmare?p=1089425#post1089425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The stat and Nightmare dice are distinct from the legacies and realm. From a design perspective, using a term like Nightmare for multiple purposes that don't intersect is a no-no, but there were several points in the design process for C20 were we had to strike a balance between respecting the previous edition and adding/changing things.<br /> <br /> As for the Nightmare Flaws, adding them back in as consequence when a Nightmare die rolls '1' sounds fun, but it would significantly slow the progression toward Bedlam. If you run it that way put up a post and let me know how it plays, I'd be interested to hear about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As they are now, Nightmare Dice don't have anything to do with Nightmare and the name is confusing. They should probably be called Wyld Dice or something more in-keeping with what they represent. <br /> <br /> Maybe the old Nightmare Flaws could just replace the Derangements system (since Derangements no longer appear in the game)? When your psyche breaks, the monstrous chaos of the Fomorians creeps in and makes you into something darker. <br /> <br /> Bedlam, meanwhile, is the loss of self-control in the face of Glamour--and doesn't have to have anything to do with the Fomorian Dream.<br /> <br /> In fact, I think that's exactly how I'm going to houserule it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}